.TH LANDHORSE 1 "2026-10-03" "landhorse" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
landhorse \- manage passwords, keyrings, PGP and SSH keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B landhorse
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ run
.RI [ \-\-category\fR=\fIKEY ]]
.br
.B landhorse
.RI [ options ]
.B list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B landhorse
is a graphical manager for the passwords stored in your keyrings (through the
freedesktop.org Secret Service, such as gnome\-keyring), your GnuPG keys and your OpenSSH
keys. It replaces GNOME's Passwords and Keys (Seahorse), and is also installed as
.BR seahorse .
.PP
The window shows the type of thing on the left, a list of that type in the middle, and
the details of the selected item on the right.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Open the window. This is the default.
.B \-\-category
selects a category on startup, by the key that
.B list
prints.
.TP
.B list
Print every category and item to standard output, and exit. It only reads.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-file= FILE
Read configuration from
.I FILE
instead of
.IR ~/.config/landhorse/landhorse.yml .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level= LEVEL
Logging level: debug, info, warn or error.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Show all options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/landhorse/landhorse.yml
Optional configuration. It can hide a backend, point at another GnuPG home or SSH
directory, or set the keyservers used to publish and revoke keys. Without a keyserver
setting, landhorse uses the same keyservers as Seahorse: the
.B keyservers
key of the
.B org.gnome.crypto.pgp
GSettings schema.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpg (1),
.BR ssh\-keygen (1),
.BR secret\-tool (1)
